{"title":"2020 USOJMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Angle-Chasing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Angle-Chasing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex quadrilateral inscribed in a circle and satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/d/99d54e5007a86f10a66eefce47692313be1f95a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA &lt; AB = BC &lt; CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"188\" height=\"13\" />. Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen on sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61ed62dbca41685d2f8b353db5a2cc78dee1da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE \\perp AC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edf8c99ea2f1428adee96a02db580e9e7ebc8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF \\parallel BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/1908d81b5adf8f69f4b64e43c2352ab8b7fa9fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FB = FD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/2120382734c1283fcc73d7f6d748111388daec38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABCD)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7387ef3aa3162cea3e516216d4ed946506bd30d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/2120382734c1283fcc73d7f6d748111388daec38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABCD)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><b>Claim: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd95a08eb67cbe9067e1db482c50c2140f2644e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GH || FE || BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" /></b>\n</p><p>By Pascal's on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/2/26210640d6c314e223960f1fb0e7bf1f86744b74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GDCBAH$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" />, we see that the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7a248cfd02095e2a009f811d5732a9bea9d595.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are collinear. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/9/eb9a2f8064e21664080fd3fc9789af308c5c3e33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE || BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/5/ec50ae0dde69d08266c6b82cc8ff6738b7c50f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG || BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> as well. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Note that since all cyclic trapezoids are isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fef4c28e7b3e3404daddc25e51bbe104d0aa808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HB = GC$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/7/fb71d5ba363a314c0343efdd9a19aafe8070c75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/2075232cf05b89c80e4a5c39d5ab9f5918cab069.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EB \\perp AC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d7b7e1766562c5e2a1b3308a57a253f6237e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EA = EC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, from which we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aa034442fbaa56732cb01b187855d19775d4f42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DGCA$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is an isosceles trapezoid and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18ade2323dd7531ef82c97cdd192ce6dd761eaca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA = GC$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/c/07c41e45fc9064bf7b39c6c82922dffaca80d781.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DA = GC = HB$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/0/a7036fd94bdb46f6a7ed42f32b82513055bab007.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BHAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" /> is an isosceles trapezoid, from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/0/1908d81b5adf8f69f4b64e43c2352ab8b7fa9fa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FB = FD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />, as desired. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d23c047ad3f53d68366af14fa5d46ac1f2379e44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G=\\overline{FE}\\cap\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/8/3b863e09bca6890fe0eee72825dc343319713268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G=\\overline{AC}\\cap\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />. Now let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/733cbff7cbd7638f10f0180a6773f0724177b2ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\angle ACE$\" width=\"89\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e013ca5eb757df9558f4c263788474915ad9c82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=\\angle BCA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f69c5a02f2548972c63d3df0943c308295cfe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA=BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/7/0e7ff7c9090d69dc3bf911a87ac0ad9024ecba8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}\\perp \\overline{AC}$\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cc64d695e60b2ce5256f22259d4a9dca7cd7176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=EC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/5/655c26605a513f3e11d97ea717b732a2c66bc34e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle EAC =\\angle ECA = x$\" width=\"169\" height=\"13\" />. From cyclic quadrilateral ABCD, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/d/e5de82b523b32b0d04605b4e2cfaf43f6ff45aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD = \\angle ACD = x$\" width=\"171\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/f/09f69c5a02f2548972c63d3df0943c308295cfe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BA=BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/4727f8dc2bf8ca920c68f674baf86878b7ad1e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCA = \\angle BAC = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"168\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Now from cyclic quadrilateral ABC and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/a/45ac358880a313a12f15fd8ab539c70ae1a11cc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{FE}\\parallel \\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99bd0993f70be90b411711bccc1304864f54d084.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FAC = \\angle BAC = \\pi - \\angle BCD = \\pi - \\angle FED$\" width=\"363\" height=\"13\" />. Thus F, A, D, and E are concyclic, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b46e035914e867de22913ebb335b8cd7b90b643.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DFG = \\angle DAE = \\angle DAC - \\angle EAC = \\angle DBC - x$\" width=\"409\" height=\"13\" /> Let this be statement 1.\n</p><p>Now since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/0/7d0637d2916a8e8b70dcd530c39813216a7b72df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AH}\\perp \\overline {BH}$\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />, triangle ABC gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d65dc437d785c0e223ac60e64601011c01233d32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAH + \\angle ABG = \\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"173\" height=\"33\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d486032e22beb5fff138ff0462426ffbd45103a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y+x+\\angle GBE=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"158\" height=\"33\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da4731eb8265cd2ad008c225b069a06fbb80237.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GBE = \\frac{\\pi}{2}-x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"159\" height=\"33\" />. \n</p><p>Right triangle BHC gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/0/810893d1f35c5707426b471d7dfa7f975ad8e05d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle HBC = \\frac{\\pi}{2}-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"129\" height=\"33\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d51a61f4f20a307c4b54f6e2650f43c78116b79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}\\parallel \\overline{FE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d4b5e63ab1f0bac5c7d83f4e5a49e7cda753214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BEG=\\angle HBC = \\frac{\\pi}{2}-y.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"213\" height=\"33\" /> \n</p><p>Now triangle BGE gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/4/8b48c4a3aa9bb74a38c2da6e5130455f7b9d82c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BGE = \\pi - \\angle BEG - \\angle GBE = \\pi - (\\frac{\\pi}{2}-y)-(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-x-y)=x+2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"557\" height=\"33\" />. But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e794bef35604d02750f755311f00ca3912ef91a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FGB = \\angle BGE$\" width=\"136\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/f/ecff03fb3db648b2ef9759a59eefa60d2dd142b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FGB=x+2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />. Using triangle FGD and statement 1 gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e284912f3809fa203f5915eb74008d5e6a23cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\angle FDG &amp;= \\pi - \\angle DFG - \\angle FGB \\\\ &amp;= \\pi - (\\angle DBC - x) - (x + 2y) \\\\ &amp;= \\pi - (\\angle GBE + \\angle EBC - x) - (x + 2y) \\\\ &amp;= \\pi - ([\\frac{\\pi}{2}-x-y]+[\\frac{\\pi}{2}-y]-x)-(x+2y) \\\\ &amp;= x \\\\ &amp;= \\angle FBD\\end{align*}\" width=\"415\" height=\"153\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e33787a51d92ecebfaed2ca4fa3ae4540e9f6a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FDB = \\angle FBD$\" width=\"138\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/4/a94efde019211a7a014f8559e4f2cf8786420133.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{FB=FD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" /> as desired.<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~MortemEtInteritum\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Angle-Chasing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Angle-Chasing)\">Solution 3 (Angle-Chasing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Angle-Chasing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e37c7f3da8c2c66e7b788ad1da24dd33c27736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FB=FD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" /> is equivalent to proving that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/c/7ec1d921639180c5cc7b15901f0b684f216955cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FBD= \\angle FDB$\" width=\"138\" height=\"12\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/5/d55724bb11eefc3c7ea0d4d2601d2318f693d3e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FBD=\\angle ACD$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" /> because quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic. Also note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/0/050b6288e0e7abe6d282f9c22bdda0125e545b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC=\\angle ACB$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/4/5f4c25cb7b6078137512af0317bd262160bd0319.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=BC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/c/8cc64d695e60b2ce5256f22259d4a9dca7cd7176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=EC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />, which follows from the facts that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/1/b61ed62dbca41685d2f8b353db5a2cc78dee1da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE \\perp AC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c99bbe74cccdc92b249d376f13d9429d41a8b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b0c41f271c177a0af9b9adc6bc6387f478b0ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAE= \\angle ACE= \\angle ACD= \\angle FBD$\" width=\"296\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, we would like to prove that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/2/a4280b51205a516de3a891f86968342518b9a806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FBD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is similar to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16496008e00789fb4615ae746ae82befaf89ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. In order for this to be true, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/d/eed6106eb0d2f3ae22644d7dcd663d4dd7054b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BFD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3eddba1b3d73e20a58d18dd47b4615d258155333.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEC$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/a/ffa3b7259c998cffa903a1c8c6912d977d19d7b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFD$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> must equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410914bb0ff2a9961ffd2cf13393f5ed8d9fefae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AED$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />. In order for this to be true, then quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f26e85ac9c958d93ff103a7c6045f2c98590081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFED$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> must be cyclic. Using the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edf8c99ea2f1428adee96a02db580e9e7ebc8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF \\parallel BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/5117bfe4e7b062db7fab26642f395228191f4ded.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFE= \\angle ABC$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a3dcbc4cb2fee38679867573c68533139bbe5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FED= \\angle BCE$\" width=\"137\" height=\"12\" />, and thus we have proved that quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f26e85ac9c958d93ff103a7c6045f2c98590081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFED$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is cyclic. Therefore, triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b82e498d73b4f593760f1f47f8db58b956368b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FDB$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> is similar to isosceles triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c16496008e00789fb4615ae746ae82befaf89ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> from AA and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e37c7f3da8c2c66e7b788ad1da24dd33c27736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FB=FD$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>-xXINs1c1veXx\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>BE is perpendicular bisector of AC, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b8423758af69cef9f9e0cdc3c13cc583fe6d181a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ACE = \\angle EAC$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />. FE is parallel to BC and ABCD is cyclic, so AFED is also cyclic. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/9/519c5b7d3368c58d1ee506398deefe93b77d95f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AFD = \\angle AED = 2 \\angle ACE = 2 \\angle FBD$\" width=\"315\" height=\"13\" />. Hence, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c8f574b420cf8489f2647752193ca576c014f78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FBD = \\angle BDF$\" width=\"138\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/2/0e274b8d7047d55b176172b066ca9218db1947b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD = FB$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>Mathdummy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/b/bdbb8dbfdd7a6ea228c1c8bc743a92ba4f7344ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GD \\perp DB$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/2/25266d5416855484ab10a25e42558ebb85ed404f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H = GD \\cap EB$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"119\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/5/ab526cc0a7dcd78e0372efb23571196e0bbd18db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADB} = \\angle{EDB} = 90^{\\circ} - \\angle{ABE} \\implies \\triangle{DAE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"378\" height=\"18\" /> is the orthic triangle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/1/f61421173028897dbeee6e4c54e28c3a12c00938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{HGB}$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/8360f78d23bb55e76184817a204a029c7165dbe7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$GB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> and lies on the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/29501a90018e83d6d3e88b1f83bdfb71e692561e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\perp$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204a6f5a6757f5da4c1b3035ad8d806769744e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abb5588023cfa1ac14643e9778699f03eecc57a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$J$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7baf95ecafc2d7791788ec79aeeae390d60b119.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, connect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac524cb86f8a88bf8a0015800f3e7a418b73db17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE, SD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />.\nDenote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe192cd72d36a47ff0ddddcdf788a3fd6783268.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BCA}=\\alpha; AB=BC, \\angle{BAC}=\\angle{BCA}=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"361\" height=\"18\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/9/349456d96e7054678ffb47de94c04ceff5e6406b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AJF}=\\angle{ACB}=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"170\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f6074d57fbc8407d5305283e17c111135919d7ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{AJF}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b311c7054e7d6d8596c8c2e732156f4d776b77e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EJS}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"14\" /> are vertical angle, so they are equal to each other. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/68118c6c533d251a6d653095d2567d856138591b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE\\bot{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/1/881a1b1afe7073ea6ed8fb328288ba973be1ed2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{JES}=90^{\\circ}-\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb9feb7c282e557c268326184b2b269bd1613631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EFB}=\\angle{AJF}+\\angle{FAJ}=2\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"255\" height=\"16\" />, we can express <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25fbc792023832d68c8453792001d2b0dd02418.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FBE}=180^{\\circ}-2\\alpha-(90^{\\circ}-\\alpha)=90^{\\circ}-\\alpha= \\angle{FEB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"421\" height=\"20\" />, leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/3/4f361072b579456e4da7ec3c3c5c4d508980e9c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE=FB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Notice that quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f26e85ac9c958d93ff103a7c6045f2c98590081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFED$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> is a cyclic quadrilateral since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff6b4755ef38939fc6e7ed3764d3f0b9b44006a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ADE}+\\angle{AFE}=\\angle{ADE}+\\angle{ABC}=180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"353\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5b0f349472dc706e5745276baf67deac08f02e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ECA}=\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/e/a9ed5c36e61c791a76abb9e11b93516cae8e49fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{AES}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/9/8394edc044efdb5419f1bfc7c69b359c33b10d82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CES}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5edef24b91fbbbc3e567f5c6f717ece6ae921e27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AS=AS,\\angle{ASE}=\\angle{BSE}, SE=SE(SAS)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"354\" height=\"20\" />, so we can get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/e/19e92164016f6d11f3253dc92fffe519f959eb50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EAS}=\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> \nLet the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/2/5f26e85ac9c958d93ff103a7c6045f2c98590081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFED$\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />\nNow notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821523cfd9fda4e376ebfb301e873e58f4bb803b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{QE}=\\widehat{QE}, \\angle{QAE}=\\angle{QDE}=\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"264\" height=\"23\" />; similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f97b13582cea18a9dfc4fce75ed81e0452dd19b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widehat{FQ}=\\widehat{FQ}; \\angle{FDQ}=\\angle{FAQ}=\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"264\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/2/0b2559070dc0b90e94d69613b353625bc223a5d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{FDE}=\\alpha+\\beta; \\angle{FED}=\\angle{BCD}=\\alpha+\\beta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"345\" height=\"18\" />, it leads to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd7971fa19b6d39340b9f1ec48b0516ac2fd04d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD=FE$\" width=\"82\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/d/43dbf3c96c78e412a460eea9451c0d9fa606dc4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE=FB;FD=FE, DF=BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"265\" height=\"18\" /> as desired\n~bluesoul\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USOJMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO\">2020 USAJMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=176&amp;year=2020\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_USAJMO_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2020 USAJMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAJMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAJMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017162704\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.081 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 723/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1326/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 23458/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   18.735      1 -total\n 73.20%   13.714      1 Template:USAJMO_newbox\n 25.68%    4.812      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18967:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017162704 and revision id 199253. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}